timestamp=2026-11-04T09:46:28.199Z level=INFO run=92c8de62 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# What about negative quantities or something else? No. Maybe dispatches with extremely high quantities that were \"written off\" as loss? Unusual, but let us look for outliers.\nimport csv\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\nproducts = {}\nwith open('/app/dataset/product_catalog.csv') as f:\n    r = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in r:\n        pid = row['product_id']\n        ean = row['ean_code']\n        price = float(row['unit_price'].replace(',', '.'))\n        weight = float(row['unit_weight_kg'].replace(',', '.'))\n        cat = row['storage_category'].strip().lower()\n        prod = {'price': price, 'weight': weight, 'cat': cat, 'name': row['name']}\n        products[pid] = prod\n        products[ean] = prod\n\nwith open('/app/dataset/warehouse_dispatches.csv') as f:\n    r = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for d in r:\n        pid = d['product_id']\n        prod = products.get(pid)\n        qty = int(d['quantity'])\n        if prod:\n            val = qty * prod['price']\n            if val > 5000:  # very high\n                print(d, prod['name'], val)\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
